    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2036808216898687080",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/2036808216898687080",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/2036808216898687080",
      "text": "[3:05PM] #VI #TrafficUpdate \n\nDescending from Mcwen bridge inward Bonny camp roundabout has an appreciable vehicular movement.\n\nTraffic Inward and outward Ahmadu Bello way is on the high side  but moving  slowly as a result of an ongoing event at Onikan coupled with  closing hour rush and traffic light at intersections point.\n\nAhmadu Bello by IMB inward and outward Coastal road is a moving traffic coupled with closing hour rush.\n\nTraffic inward Eko Hotel roundabout is moving slowly steady but traffic light delay at alternating point same as the return  journey.\n\nVehicular movement from Bonny camp under bridge enroute Kofo Abayomi is moving while inward Oniru Kilimajaro is a moving traffic.\n\nDescending  from Akin Adeshola bridge enroute  Law School down to  Civic center is busy but moving with high influx coupled with alternating point at intersection.\n\nCivic Centre Inward BJ1004 to School corner inward Sandfield is very much appreciable.\n\nSandfield enroute Lekki is encouraging while traffic is building up approaching Lekki intersection.\n\nThe return from Lekki Phase 1 to Sandfiled is moving well while traffic building up approaching Sandfield bus stop as a result of bus stop activities and closing hour rush.\n\nSandfield  enroute School corner down to BJ  traffic is building up.\n\nBj 1004 to Civic Center inward Ramp bridge is  on the high side as a result of closing hour rush coupled with extended traffic from Falomo.\n\nCivic center inward Law school, Akin Adeshola, Kilimanjaro connecting Kofo, Bonny  down to Mcwen bridge is very much on the high side with a slow movement as a result of  extended backlog from Onikan due to an event ongoing at that corridor  coupled closing hour rush.\n\nThere are slight traffic delays at alternation points at this moment.",
